{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxnEAdsdN9QQwg7ZHXtQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four steps are done, and the read-back confirms the rule is enabled and the panel title changed.\n\n- **Data view:** The time field of \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\" is `timestamp`.\n- **Dashboard:** \"S4-b3ae9bc7 Web logs\" has two panels: \"Requests over time\" and \"Requests by response code\".\n- **Alert rule:** \"S4-b3ae9bc7 5xx errors\" checks every minute. It fires when more than 10 requests with a response code from 500 to 599 arrive within 5 minutes. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n- **Panel edit:** The second panel is now titled \"Responses by code\".\n- **Read-back:** The rule shows `enabled: true` with status `ok`.\n\nThe `response` field is a string, so the rule matches 500–599 as a text range on `response.keyword`. That works for three-digit codes. I haven't tested the rule against real 5xx data.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_read_input_tokens":20804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534},"output_tokens":339,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da1e72d-e9d9-58d9-b388-fca8d0eba393","uuid":"8ded294d-035c-4306-922a-8fd10e0b910d","timestamp":"2026-10-12T18:01:14.099Z","request_id":"req_011CfxnEAPVWajUjnvn1GMSY"}
